DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvffss__ggeettnneewwffssiidd() function allocates a new file system identifier for
     the mount point given.  File systems typically call vvffss__ggeettnneewwffssiidd() in
     their mount routine in order to acquire a unique ID within the system
     which can later be used to uniquely identify the file system via calls
     such as vfs_getvfs(9).

     The actual _f_s_i_d is made up of two 32 bit integers, that are stored in the
     _s_t_a_t_f_s structure of _m_p.  The first integer is unique in the set of
     mounted file systems, while the second holds the file system type.

     typedef struct fsid {
             int32_t val[2];
     } fsid_t;

